      "credentials": {
        "postgres": {
          "name": "Neon GTM"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Sprint 14 patch: a queue left over is normal. Contact Finder takes contact.max_accounts_per_run (10) per run,\n// and Select Contact Batch tops the queue up to that cap. Fail only when the queue is not moving:\n// accounts are waiting and neither engine pass of this run wrote a contact.\n// Note: GTM Engine: Error Alerts fires for production runs only; a manual run shows the red node instead.\nconst row = $input.first().json;\nconst n = Number(row.queued_left || 0);\nlet runs = row.last_runs;\nif (typeof runs === 'string') { try { runs = JSON.parse(runs); } catch (e) { runs = []; } }\nruns = Array.isArray(runs) ? runs : [];\nconst written = runs.reduce((s, r) => s + Number((r && r.contacts_written) || 0), 0);\nif (n > 0 && written === 0) throw new Error('GTM Run: ' + n + ' accounts queued but no contacts written this run. Check GTM Contact Finder.');\nreturn [{ json: Object.assign({\n  status: n > 0 ? 'ok_queue_draining' : 'ok',\n  queued_left: n,\n  contacts_written_this_run: written,\n  next_step: written > 0 ? 'Run Clay Email Queue, the Clay waterfall and Clay Email Import, then GTM Run again to draft.' : 'Nothing new to enrich.'\n}, row) }];\n"
      },
      "id": "ec674cf6-049d-4f4f-adad-ffff455c2130",
      "name": "Fail If Queue Left",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        560,
        750
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## GTM Run\nOne click runs the batch in order: Gig Finder, Neon Sync, Engine, Contact Finder, Engine, Neon Sync.\n\n**How:** every step hangs off Manual Trigger and runs top to bottom (execution order v1), each waiting for its sub-workflow. Keep the steps stacked in this order; moving one changes the order.\n**Gig Finder (Sprint 15)** runs first because gig posts go stale fastest. It continues on error, so the gig lane never blocks the engine chain.\n**Cycle (ADR-112):** GTM Run finds contacts, then Clay Email Queue, Clay waterfall and Clay Email Import, then GTM Run again drafts.\n**Fails on purpose** only when accounts are queued and no contact was written (Contact Finder stuck). A queue left over is normal: 10 accounts per run.\n**On failure:** GTM Engine: Error Alerts (production runs only).",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 520
      },
      "id": "23ade2f6-944c-4fd7-a613-433141fad116",
